{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-132290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/797cddb4ea3cb41959df88e56517e9ee71e76e3cd08a9a93d2957b9792d14abb.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-\\frac{2x}{3},$ $y=\\frac{4x}{3}$ and $y=\\frac{x}{3}+3,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132290" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/0e69b1cb480b87216273db4336adff57cbf9d9bc450aac4b0cdb58b1ae63f6f7.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le 0,\\,-\\frac{2x}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{3}+3}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{4x}{3}\\le y\\le \\frac{x}{3}+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{-2x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{4x/3}^{x/3+3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132290" "field" 