ext{d}y\\,\\text{d}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2,$ and the lines $y=x+2,$ $x=-2$ and $x=2.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/019f0f9f83ddf323d543d109677335cb3ae72a200baf834453a0eca16a9353ba.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/d222e86f6af7c3ed2b35711114c9062d6f0c9b0f2551aa44cac33318c6e5813f.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,x+2\\le y\\le \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\\le y\\le x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-132292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{1}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{{x}^{2}/2+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}/2+2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-x,$ $y=2$ and $y=\\frac{x}{2}.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/990f2180e92ffa9ae0b77a7c8c4aae284cacf03f7a7a62b1ed0b56f24705d671.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/db7fe0aa7b746eab86c011545ec37d59d8f225f02a9fc6f4388754e1c528db8c.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}x\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-132291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{2}^{x/2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{2}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{x/2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=-6{x}^{2}+24x-17$ and lines $y=6x-5,$ $x=3,$ and $y=1.$\nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/fe0209b3ed99aae4a1a939dfc7a8e0e400976809cc220abb1fbdf2f766c76171.png)\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c8ba7d6923e2e4ef9ee528c48a8f5664ec10e4f05a13dad941713600d93ddfe5.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 6x-5}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,1\\le y\\le -6{x}^{2}+24x-17}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-82355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82355" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{6x-5}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{-6{x}^{2}+24x-17}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y={e}^{x},$ $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$  and the lines $y=1-x$  and $y=1+e-x.$ \nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/4854afc35aff7cfb47ba09481f975b22e41f3309b08a2ba7c409a4bbd32c8601.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/50c5b7a864099f512515ab2db4c1596382883e93f7d4b23b9d16b91e42e3021b.png)\n\n   \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-x\\le y\\le {e}^{x}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 1+e-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82074" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-82074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1+x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e+x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e+x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{2}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82074" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{{e}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1+e-x}f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/a4515d2789a9b5c7a08210c0ef2611e7b6e661850b1fa822016b880427088bae.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y={x}^{2},$ and the lines $y=2-x$ and $y=x,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,x=-\\sqrt{y} \\\\ y=2-x & \\,⟹\\,x=2-y \\\\ y=x & \\,⟹\\,x=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/78aa61f11856dbf35287a0af016b56744fec354d6c4e64690a1a6fe466f164e8.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le y}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,-\\sqrt{y}\\le x\\le 2-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-132385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2-y}^{-\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{-\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{2-y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y}}^{2-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y={e}^{x},$ and the lines $y=1-x$ and $x=1.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={e}^{x} & \\,⟹\\,x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\ y=1-x & \\,⟹\\,x=1-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/0c61de3680b68dcf16267483fe1a51f0ef0e4c8247104215ae319d6c01b7a571.png)\n\n  \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c2a3cd01f74a2adb96e13212916dbb1b4476040d701ccd755258bd22fdefa5de.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,1-y\\le x\\le 1}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡y\\le x\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132391" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-132391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{{e}^{y}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132391" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y={2}^{x},$ $y=\\sqrt{x}$  and lines $y=1$ and $y=6-x.$\nExpress ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={2}^{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={log}_{2}⁡y \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2} \\\\ y=6-x & \\,⟹\\,x=6-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/fe95bc4ca8c687c79fe1c475eb1d8001d71a41ba34e076ad7fdfa8391cb08839.png)\n\n   \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/099c35cbab4dfdd4a94207ed950fbdca8b8e766a612fb5e665e7d443d75ec050.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,{log}_{2}⁡y\\le x\\le {y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le y\\le 4,\\,{log}_{2}⁡y\\le x\\le 6-y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-82137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}{\\int }_{2}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}^{4}{\\int }_{{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{1}^{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{\\operatorname{log}⁡2}^{4}{\\int }_{{2}^{y}}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{{log}_{2}⁡y}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-37757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/3fb6039f0a1de69d41644d7153d205062e85cdfce7cdb6b6270d952f2dbab6c3.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=x+6,$ $y=2x,$ and $y=3x,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-37757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2} \\\\ y=x+6 & \\,⟹\\,x=y-6 \\\\ y=3x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c453d46a1f0cd6e6ddfa926de471fe38663df2bd86b9cdf4e58ce8d42462774a.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 9,\\,\\frac{y}{3}\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,9\\le y\\le 12,\\,y-6\\le x\\le \\frac{y}{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\int }_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{9}^{12}{\\int }_{y-6}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-37757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-37757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-37757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\int }_{y-6}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{9}^{12}{\\int }_{y-6}^{y/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\int }_{y-6}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{9}^{12}{\\int }_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\int }_{y/3}^{6-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{9}^{12}{\\int }_{y/2}^{y/3}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\int }_{y/3}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{9}^{12}{\\int }_{y/3}^{y-6}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\int }_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{9}^{12}{\\int }_{y-6}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-37757" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{9}{\\int }_{y/3}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{9}^{12}{\\int }_{y-6}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y=-x,$ $y=6-4x$ and $y=2x.$ Express ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's write our equations in terms of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=-x & \\,⟹\\,x=-y \\\\ y=6-4x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4} \\\\ y=2x & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{y}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/08237d1ca2e01d0cf620dfa06a4265d8053b7ee34d0b65036aad7d5734726e1c.png)\n\n \n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c756dc7924fc4c116601da907eb3b767b8a40647e063c146dad83b0ea660933b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\frac{y}{2}\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-132397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{3/2-y/4}^{y/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{3/2-y/4}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] ["math" "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{6-4y}^{-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2y}^{6-4y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y/2}^{3/2-y/4}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${∬}_{|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}\\,\\,6(x+y)\\,dA=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's draw a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/c9072d2b8f1b49770403280af13d3d8e681247f168e796c056eb697fe28b8ba9.png)\n\n  \n\nThe  region $D={(x,y)|\\,\\,|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}$ can be  partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/d16296029378c7adb891affba63683971ff972b5ed0268641ac3b677c694b5f8.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le 2-y}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y\\le x\\le y+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{|x-1|+|y|\\le 1}6(x+y)^{2}\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}6(x+y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}6(x+y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}6(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{-y}^{y+2}6(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[3(x+y)^{2}]_{y}^{2-y}\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}[3(x+y)^{2}]_{-y}^{y+2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3(4-4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}3(2y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =3{[4y-\\frac{4{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{1}+4{[(y+1)^{3}]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =8+4 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82223" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-82223" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82223" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82223" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/a4265e8993b5c7ea5756fe55facd5313e5c2237cbdbc851195ebf458e5246060.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/33a38da74b282f0ec1fb2fae9cb155feb2a5fd39128c7607b80c6b84fedd29b4.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,x-1\\le y\\le 3-x}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,3-x\\le y\\le x-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{x-1}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{3-x}^{x-1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{x-1}^{3-x}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{3-x}^{x-1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}[(x-1)^{2}-(3-x)^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(8-4x)\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(4x-8)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(8x-2{x}^{2}){|}_{1}^{2}+(2{x}^{2}-8x){|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =8(2-1)-2({2}^{2}-{1}^{2})+2({4}^{2}-{2}^{2})-8(4-2) \\\\  & =8-6+24-16 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132423" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-132423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "\\frac{55}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{55}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{71}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-132423" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/ad8d4069ab0effd57ba58ccc4bf5792d5a014b114afb086e6d4b71d69ba14d2c.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curves $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=|x|,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2x\\,dA.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/2fcb30778db2f051a7a819ae701808af59ac18d27c25a9c57ce678caa6c3ee3b.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le -x}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2x\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2x\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2x\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{-x}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{x}2x\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}2xy{|}_{{x}^{2}}^{-x}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}2xy{|}_{{x}^{2}}^{x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}2x[-x-{x}^{2}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}2x[x-{x}^{2}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{x}^{2}-2{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{-1}^{0}+{[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =((0-(-\\frac{2}{3}(-1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{4}))+((\\frac{2}{3}(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{4})-0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82360" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-82360" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82360" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82360" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/ebb0b09ffab6ffdff6a04104b09d6904302fdb7580262663b5e0c65bd3f95502.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the the curve $y=(x-1)^{2}$ and the lines $y=x+1$ and $y=3-x,$ as shown in the picture. Evaluate ${∬}_{D}2y\\,dA.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/f26c3e1bbbc268308db8d419bc799ad5349673e97c8828471997a5d36cb94d7d.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x+1}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le 3-x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2y\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}2y\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}2y\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{x+1}\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}{|}_{(x-1)^{2}}^{3-x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[(x+1)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}[(3-x)^{2}-(x-1)^{4}]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{1}+{[-\\frac{(3-x)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(x-1)^{5}}{5}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =((\\frac{8}{3}-0)-(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{5}))+((-\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{5})-(-\\frac{8}{3}-0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{15}+\\frac{32}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-82229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{106}{25}"] ["math" "\\frac{48}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{64}{15}"] ["math" "\\frac{78}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{84}{25}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82229" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{64}{15}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/13275042f8b7b74e394b3cee1350c19cfa50ddf63899066682cbd0109f42d6bf.png)\n\nEvaluate ${∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA,$ where $D$ is the region shown in the picture above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions ${D}_{1}$ and ${D}_{2},$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/648121ff2a676f6a472a6e221dffe813eca55f914aed0ca9a285bb0d4cd81ab3.png)\n\n   \n\nAs a result, we get \n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 3},\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}4xy\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}4xy\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}4xy\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[2x{y}^{2}]}_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{[2x{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2x(9-1)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}2x(9-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}16x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}18x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{2}+9{x}^{2}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =8(4-0)+9(9-4) \\\\  & =77.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82362" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bdd186fb77f2edf92954a9152d7794dcce4903c07b0892754eaba68225796fbb"} {"question" "q-82362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "112"] ["math" "44"] ["math" "77"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "q-82362" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "77"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f7a93e320ad6a8f52e62674be6eea2bc508f9cdbe13d793d13a24bbc95d558c"} {"question" "e-7198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y= 2^x,$ $y=\\sqrt{x}$  and lines $x=0$ and $y=2,$ as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of a function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/b80527fdef6f890581b8f56431e1b72a8f7eae3b41827caa16486ed9f2fd45ea.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/example-7198.json" "file_sha256" "4314699a02d915eb6ceda9c1592ebb96fcbc8eab7bff66655a574d1ab40dc067"} {"question" "e-7198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below.  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/939e46b3ed4266f3c18d3567f951276e420292781cfc414711c244f453bc4029.png)\n\n  \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x  \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2^x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq x  \\leq 4, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{{2}^{x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/example-7198.json" "file_sha256" "4314699a02d915eb6ceda9c1592ebb96fcbc8eab7bff66655a574d1ab40dc067"} {"question" "e-7199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=2+\\ln x,$  and the lines $y=1$, $x=1,$ and  $x=e,$  as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/4b0dff15fa9fa93ed61183702bff6bb443daf14b0adbf56cf4b97e3bd830ceea.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/example-7199.json" "file_sha256" "655bdb0439cdfa689dccd38558e8b670ea1aa63932ea63e333325654ba4b8404"} {"question" "e-7199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,x={e}^{y-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/2228ad860fea1e2c30d20bce749f654da02a97c65fd5e70152a07761e26f3e78.png)\n\n    \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y  \\leq 2, \\quad 1 \\leq x \\leq e \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 2 \\leq y  \\leq 3, \\quad e^{y-2} \\leq x \\leq e\\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,dA+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{{e}^{y-2}}^{e}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/example-7199.json" "file_sha256" "655bdb0439cdfa689dccd38558e8b670ea1aa63932ea63e333325654ba4b8404"} {"question" "e-7197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/1d180fd5de88ebc465df522879142e5a4c5446c758aaccde792092968078c254.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is enclosed by the curves $x=2y^3-2y$ and  $x=y^3-4y,$ and the $y$-axis, as shown in the picture. Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} \\mathrm{d}A.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/example-7197.json" "file_sha256" "deef82f51dc608edc87ed3d25fa7f0bfe0386e9592c63cea501eef87349c629c"} {"question" "e-7197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/assets/6812e8036df171e162bee49d2edcff6d4a742e7bb4f14247713bd2332c64ccc6.png)\n\n \n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: -2 \\leq y  \\leq 0, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^3\\!-\\!4y \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y  \\leq 1, \\quad 2y^3\\!-\\!2y \\leq x \\leq 0 \\bigg\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{{D}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{{D}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{3}-4y}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{y}^{3}-2y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{3}-4y}\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{2{y}^{3}-2y}^{0}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}({y}^{3}-4y)\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2y-2{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}-2{y}^{2}]}_{-2}^{0}+{[{y}^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{4}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070962/example-7197.json" "file_sha256" "deef82f51dc608edc87ed3d25fa7f0bfe0386e9592c63cea501eef87349c629c"}] "usage" {"q-37757" [] "e-7197" [] "e-7199" [] "e-7198" []} "basis" 2520 "retractions" [[17592186129553 :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/q-37757.png)\n\nConsider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the lines $y = x + 6$, $y = 2x$, and $y = 3x$, as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x, y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions."] [17592186128947 :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curves $y= 2^x$, $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and lines $x=0$ and $y=2$, as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of a function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/44c00a18090dd9acfb716d4de0839aed.png)"] [17592186128947 :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type I regions $D_1$ and $D_2$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/dfed9d77548799c30e813d5415b96807.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2^x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 1 \\leq x \\leq 4, \\quad \\sqrt x \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)f(x, y)dA &= ∬_(D_{1})f(x, y)dA + ∬_(D_{2})f(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2^{x}}f(x, y)dydx + ∫_{1}^{4}∫_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}f(x, y)dydx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128948 :question/problem "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed by the curve $y=2+\\ln x$, and the lines $y=1$, $x=1$, and $x=e$, as shown in the picture. Express the double integral of the function $f(x,y)$ over the region $D$ as a sum of repeated integrals over type II regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/90badcdff8d1723816783ecee432d5a9.png)"] [17592186128948 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n$$\ny = 2 + \\ln x \\mid ⟹x = e^{y - 2}\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/97aa046fce141be1472a9103f7079cae.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\quad 1 \\leq x \\leq e \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 2 \\leq y \\leq 3, \\quad e^{y-2} \\leq x \\leq e\\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)f(x, y)dA &= ∬_(D_{1})f(x, y)dA + ∬_(D_{2})f(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{1}^{2}∫_{1}^{e}f(x, y)dxdy + ∫_{2}^{3}∫_{e^{y - 2}}^{e}f(x, y)dxdy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128946 :question/problem "The region $D$ is enclosed by the curves $x=2y^3-2y$ and $x=y^3-4y$, and the $y$-axis, as shown in the picture. Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} \\mathrm{d}A$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/ad479776abe1b64937bf9c79c413a827.png)"] [17592186128946 :question/worked-solution "The region $D$ can be partitioned into two type II regions $D_1$ and $D_2$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1996/Source/Images/f0e34c7f4bb3ec1fc5266af37fe73361.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD_1 = \\bigg\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: -2 \\leq y \\leq 0, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq y^3\\!-\\!4y \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nD_2 = \\bigg\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\quad 2y^3\\!-\\!2y \\leq x \\leq 0 \\bigg\\}\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the additivity property of double integrals, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= ∬_(D)dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D_{1})dA + ∬_(D_{2})dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{0}∫_{0}^{y^{3} - 4y}dxdy + ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{2y^{3} - 2y}^{0}dxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{0}[x]_{0}^{y^{3} - 4y}dy + ∫_{0}^{1}[x]_{2y^{3} - 2y}^{0}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{-2}^{0}(y^{3} - 4y)dy + ∫_{0}^{1}(2y - 2y^{3})dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{4}}{4} - 2y^{2}]_{-2}^{0} + [y^{2} - \\frac{y^{4}}{2}]_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= 4 + \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186127113 17592186127114 17592186127115 17592186127116 17592186127117] "immutable_fields" [[17592186127112 :answer-field/correct] [17592186127112 :answer-field/id] [17592186127112 :answer-field/key] [17592186127112 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
